eory—developing a knight, controlling the center, and preparing castling.\n\nReason:  \nN: g1-f3 develops a knight to a strong square, increases control over the center (particularly e5 and d4), avoids premature pawn pushes, and keeps flexibility. It doesn’t commit the queen or weaken pawn structure, while enabling quick castling. It’s one of the most reliable first moves in classical chess openings.\n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
